{"_meta":{"anthropic/requiresUserInteraction":true},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"Write files through the gate (preview, then confirm)"},"description":"One-tool transactional write: send the files you want written/deleted. Without confirmDigest it compiles them against the current tree, runs the pre-apply checks and returns status `preview` with the manifestDigest and a unified diff (nothing outside .axiom/ touched). Call again with the SAME files, intent and profile plus confirmDigest=<manifestDigest> to apply atomically (when the client supports elicitation the user confirms first): pre-image verification, journal, two-phase commit, one-step rollback via axiom_rollback. If any target changed since the preview the digest changes \u2192 ERR_CONFIRM_DIGEST_MISMATCH (re-preview). Prefer it over plain file writes for multi-file or sensitive changes.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"confirmDigest":{"description":"Absent \u2192 preview; the manifestDigest returned by the preview \u2192 apply","type":"string"},"files":{"description":"Files to write (whole new content) or delete; paths are relative POSIX","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"content":{"description":"New file content; required for op write, forbidden for op delete","type":"string"},"encoding":{"description":"Encoding of `content` (default utf8)","enum":["utf8","base64"],"type":"string"},"mode":{"description":"File mode (default 0644)","enum":["0644","0755"],"type":"string"},"op":{"description":"write (default) or delete","enum":["write","delete"],"type":"string"},"path":{"description":"Relative POSIX path, NFC, no reserved names","maxLength":1024,"minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"type":"object"},"maxItems":2000,"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"intent":{"description":"Why \u2014 recorded in the Plan","maxLength":2000,"type":"string"},"keepBac